# Local commits → push to main only when asked

Work on **`main`**. After every meaningful change, **commit locally**. Do not wait for “commit”.

This supersedes feature-branch auto-push while we iterate on live `main`.

## After each task (do this without being asked)

1. **One concern per commit** (see `focused-commits-for-main.mdc`).
2. `git add` only that change. Never stage `.env.local` or secrets.
3. `git commit` on **main**. Leave unrelated dirty files unstaged.
4. **Do not push.** Local `main` may sit ahead of `origin/main`.

If the user says “don’t commit until I say”, pause until they lift it.

## When they say “push to main” / “merge to main”

1. `git status` and `git log origin/main..HEAD --oneline`.
2. Commit any leftover work that belongs with this batch (still focused commits).
3. Show the user the exact local commits that will go live.
4. `git push origin main` — **all** of those commits, in order.
5. Never `--force` / `--force-with-lease` on `main`.
6. Do **not** Netlify-deploy unless they also ask to deploy.

## Ambiguous “push”

- “**push to main**” / “**merge to main**” → `git push origin main`.
- “**push**” alone, or push a branch name other than main → **do not** push `origin/main`; ask or push only that named branch.
